  "body": "I'd like to propose that we change how `<embed>` and `<object>` load resources with a type that starts with `image/` to be like that what we have for media resources (e.g. `<video>`), and behave like [\"7.11.6 Page load processing model for media\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#read-media). This essentially means removing the special case for images in the `<embed>` and `<object>` setup steps, and will make `<embed>` and `<object>` behave more like `<iframe>` when loading images.\r\n\r\nMaking `<embed>` and `<object>` behave more like <iframe> has been a topic [before](https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/pull/948) and feels like a pretty safe change now that we're [considering deprecating](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4592) `<object>` and `<embed>` for images.",
